":"Projection of the pinned ledger; no new mathematical assessment."},"reader_comparison":{"headline_coverage":"agree","method":"Compare reported scope categories; notes remain attributed and are not adjudicated.","points":[{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":"Zero Kolmogorov–Sinai entropy is claimed; the statement gives only finite entropy.","note":null,"reading":"reading:2c0316a2190ed971dd74410a","source_term":"NARROWER — DECLARED","state":"narrower"},{"definitions_to_check":"`def FiniteKSEntropy μ T := ∃ C : ℝ, ∀ q (P : X → Fin (q+1)), Measurable P → ∃ h ≤ C, Tendsto (fun n => blockEntropy μ T P n / n) atTop (𝓝 h)`: custom; says sup of partition entropies is finite, not zero ; `HasModelWith`/`SmoothPositiveDensity`/`ConullConjugate`: custom manifold-model encoding (density of `Measure.map (extChartAt I x)` against Lebesgue in every chart, conjugacy on invariant conull sets); read as standard","gap":null,"note":"`main` gives an ergodic invertible T on a standard nonatomic probability space with `FiniteKSEntropy` (all finite-partition entropy rates exist and share one real bound) and `¬ HasSmoothPositiveVolumeModel` (no C^∞ positive-density model on any compact manifold, closed of every dimension or with boundary); the summary's zero-entropy requirement is not stated (docs: 'the paper's stronger zero-entropy conclusion is outside this statement'), so the Lean is implied by the headline but does not imply it.","reading":"reading:1190faf8775dcceaf3f4342b","source_term":"weaker-statement","state":"weaker"}],"readings":["reading:2c0316a2190ed971dd74410a","reading:1190faf8775dcceaf3f4342b"],"state":"different-scope-descriptions"},"readings":[{"availability":"recorded","credit":{"atlas_pin":"598384f431d532144d03cbabd1c5b384e1610218","authors":[{"handle":"carlostoledo1891","name":"Carlos Toledo"}],"kind":"third-party-reported","license":"MIT","method":"Every Comparator challenge re-run on Linux with nanoda switched on, decided by a preregistered rule; every family's challe